  "html": "<text-view modelid=\"63ac0ca1185ad308b0ee2cd4\" class=\"is-left\" sgpulse-type=\"component\"><template shadowroot=\"open\"><div class=\"text-inner component__inner\"><div class=\"component__header-container\"><div data-socialgoodpulse-id=\"63ac0ca1185ad308b0ee2cd4\" class=\"component text 63ac0ca1185ad308b0ee2cd4  is-left is-complete  \"><base-view type=\"component\" lowercase_component=\"text\" customclass=\"\"><template shadowroot=\"open\"><div class=\"component__header-wrapper  \"><div class=\"component__header text__header\"><div class=\"component__header-inner text__header-inner\"><div class=\"component__content\"><div tabindex=\"0\" class=\"component__body text__body\"><div class=\"component__body-inner text__body-inner\"><ul><li>Users who insert unauthorized USB drives, CDs, or DVDs run the risk of introducing malware, or compromising data stored on their device.</li><li>Policies are in place to protect an organization’s IT infrastructure. A user can face serious consequences for purposefully violating such policies.</li><li>Using outdated hardware or software makes an organization’s systems and data more vulnerable to attack.</li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></div></template></base-view></div></div></div></template></text-view>",
  "complete": true
 },
